      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Sulfur usually forms single bonds with other sulfur atoms instead of double bonds, because of the poor overlap of its orbitals. As a result it forms larger molecules and structures through catenation: S8 is a crown-like molecule (Figure 12.7)."
          }
        ]
